---
.title = "Against the tools it replaces",
.description = "What zanity finds that the linters it consolidates find, rule by rule, and how fast.",
.date = .date("2026-10-17T00:00:02"),
.layout = "page.shtml",
---

zanity replaces six linters. This page runs each of them through its own Python library, beside zanity, on the same code, and reports what each finds.
It is generated by `bench/parity/parity.py` on 2026-10-17, against zanity `06f4cb8`; see [how to rerun it](#rerun).

# Summary

Each rule has a small fixture written to trigger it. A fixture counts only if the old tool fires on it.

| Tool | Rules | Fixtures it fires on | zanity fires on | zanity misses |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [nasa-lsp](https://github.com/benomahony/nasa-lsp) | 11 | 11 | 11/11 | – |
| [testdesiderata](https://github.com/benomahony/testdesiderata) | 39 | 38 | 37/38 | `RDL002`, `FST003` |
| [mockbuster](https://github.com/benomahony/mockbuster) | 6 | 6 | 4/6 | `mocker-fixture`, `monkeypatch-fixture` |
| [dddlint](https://github.com/benomahony/dddlint) | 12 | 10 | 8/10 | `alias:module`, `forbidden:module`, `near-synonym`, `context-outlier` |
| bonsai | 11 | 10 | 6/10 | `empty-handler`, `extractable-chunk`, `long-function`, `single-impl-abstraction` |
| [nouls](https://github.com/benomahony/nouls) | 505 | – | 28/30 questions | `fixture_hides_behaviour`, `fixture_leaks_state` |

