# Inference

nouls asks a model 30 named questions and one question per error-catalogue family, 475 in all. `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` was not set, so neither nouls nor `zanity check --infer` ran; this compares the questions. The list comes from nouls' own config loader.

| nouls question | zanity --infer question | In zanity |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `boundary_error` | `boundary-error` | yes |
| `check_then_act` | `check-then-act` | yes |
| `cryptic_error` | `cryptic-error` | yes |
| `docstring_drift` | `comment-drift` | yes |
| `fixture_hides_behaviour` | – | **no** |
| `fixture_leaks_state` | – | **no** |
| `misleading_error` | `misleading-error` | yes |
| `missing_authorisation` | `missing-authorisation` | yes |
| `mixed_abstraction` | `mixed-abstraction` | yes |
| `name_behaviour_mismatch` | `name-behaviour-mismatch` | yes |
| `non_idempotent_retry` | `non-idempotent-retry` | yes |
| `partial_failure` | `partial-failure` | yes |
| `query_with_side_effect` | `query-with-side-effect` | yes |
| `relaxed_warnings` | `weakened-check` | yes |
| `test_hard_to_write` | `heavy-setup-test` | yes |
| `test_nondeterministic` | `flaky-test` | yes |
| `test_not_automated` | `manual-test` | yes |
| `test_not_behavioural` | `hollow-test` | yes |
| `test_not_composable` | `combinatorial-test` | yes |
| `test_not_inspiring` | `trivial-test` | yes |
| `test_not_isolated` | `order-dependent-test` | yes |
| `test_not_predictive` | `self-mocking-test` | yes |
| `test_not_specific` | `unfocused-test` | yes |
| `test_slow` | `slow-test` | yes |
| `test_structure_sensitive` | `implementation-coupled-test` | yes |
| `test_unreadable` | `unreadable-test` | yes |
| `unconstructive_error` | `unconstructive-error` | yes |
| `unit_mismatch` | `unit-mismatch` | yes |
| `unscheduled_static_analysis` | `unscheduled-analysis` | yes |
| `vague_error` | `vague-error` | yes |

Of nouls' 475 catalogue questions, 103 (22%) are about a family a deterministic zanity rule detects, so zanity answers them without a model. zanity asks no question per family.

# Speed

On an M3 Max whose endpoint security slows every file open by a binary Apple didn't sign, which taxes zanity and the Python tools alike.

## From the command line

The whole corpus, 5 runs after a warm-up, with [hyperfine](https://github.com/sharkdp/hyperfine). The tools ran through the same adapters as above. Cold zanity starts each run with an empty cache.

| Command | Mean | ± | Fastest | Against zanity, all rules, cold |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| nasa-lsp | 995 ms | 17 ms | 983 ms | 4.7× |
| testdesiderata | 1.37 s | 35 ms | 1.34 s | 6.5× |
| mockbuster | 456 ms | 7 ms | 448 ms | 2.1× |
| dddlint | 755 ms | 10 ms | 742 ms | 3.5× |
| bonsai | 23.33 s | 324 ms | 23.02 s | 109.7× |
| zanity, mapped rules, cold | 217 ms | 5 ms | 210 ms | 1.0× |
| zanity, mapped rules, warm | 157 ms | 13 ms | 143 ms | 0.7× |
| zanity, all rules, cold | 213 ms | 5 ms | 205 ms | 1.0× |
| zanity, all rules, warm | 143 ms | 3 ms | 141 ms | 0.7× |
| the five tools, one after another | 26.91 s |  |  | 126.5× |

## As language servers

rich's `console.py`, 2,698 lines, alone in a workspace; the median of 5. First: from starting the server to diagnostics for the opened file. Save: from a change and save to fresh diagnostics. nouls' server needs `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` and did not run.

| Server | First | Save | Diagnostics |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| nasa-lsp | 297 ms | 64 ms | 132 |
| dddlint | 409 ms | 48 ms | 14 |
| bonsai | 2.00 s | 1.60 s | 195 |
| zanity | 139 ms | 170 ms | 72 |

# [Rerun]($heading.id('rerun'))

The harness needs checkouts of the tools beside zanity's (or `ZANITY_PARITY_SOURCES` naming their parent), each synced with `uv sync`, and hyperfine.

```sh
zig build
python3 bench/parity/parity.py   # scores, times, and writes this page
python3 bench/parity/page.py     # writes this page again from bench/parity/results.json
```
